  {
    "content": "# Blog API

Generated by chz-nest. This is a complete NestJS + TypeORM REST API with PostgreSQL.

Interactive documentation is served at \`/api/docs\` when the app is running.

## Quick start

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
npm install
npm run seed
npm run start:dev
\`\`\`

The API is mounted at \`/api\`. Set \`PORT\` in \`.env\` to change the listening port.

## Authentication

JWT access tokens are required for protected routes. Tokens are sent as \`Authorization: Bearer <token>\`. Refresh tokens rotate on every successful refresh and are stored as SHA-256 hashes.

Roles: \`admin\` (Administrator), \`user\` (User), \`editor\` (Editor)

\`passwordHash\` is selected out of normal queries, excluded from serialization, and never accepted by generic entity DTOs.

## Routes

| Method | Path | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/health\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/auth/register\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/auth/login\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/auth/logout\` | authenticated |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/auth/me\` | authenticated |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/auth/refresh\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/users/change-password\` | authenticated |
| \`PATCH\` | \`/api/users/me\` | authenticated |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/users\` | admin |
| \`PATCH\` | \`/api/users/:id/roles\` | admin |
| \`DELETE\` | \`/api/users/:id\` | admin |

### Post

A published article written by a user.

Table: \`posts\` · ownership column: \`ownerId\`

| Method | Path | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/posts\` | public |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/posts/:id\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/posts\` | authenticated |
| \`PATCH\` | \`/api/posts/:id\` | owner |
| \`DELETE\` | \`/api/posts/:id\` | roles: admin |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/posts/:id/restore\` | roles: admin |

### Tag

A label attached to posts.

Table: \`tags\`

| Method | Path | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/tags\` | public |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/tags/:id\` | public |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/tags\` | roles: admin, editor |
| \`PATCH\` | \`/api/tags/:id\` | roles: admin, editor |
| \`DELETE\` | \`/api/tags/:id\` | roles: admin |

### Comment

A reader response on a post.

Table: \`comments\` · ownership column: \`ownerId\`

| Method | Path | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/comments\` | authenticated |
| \`GET\` | \`/api/comments/:id\` | authenticated |
| \`POST\` | \`/api/comments\` | authenticated |
| \`PATCH\` | \`/api/comments/:id\` | owner |
| \`DELETE\` | \`/api/comments/:id\` | roles: admin |

## Querying

List endpoints accept:

| Parameter | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| \`page\`, \`limit\` | Pagination; defaults 1 and 20, maximum 100 |
| \`search\` | Case-insensitive contains search across the configured text fields (all string/text fields when none are configured) |
| \`sort\` | Whitelisted field; prefix with \`-\` for descending or \`+\` for ascending |
| \`order\` | \`ASC\` or \`DESC\` when \`sort\` has no prefix |
| \`<field>\` | Contains match for string/text, exact match otherwise |
| \`<field>Gte\`, \`<field>Lte\` | Inclusive ranges for numbers and dates |
| \`withDeleted\` | Administrators only; include soft-deleted rows |

Responses are wrapped as \`{ data, meta: { page, limit, total, totalPages } }\` on paginated entities.

## Ownership

When an operation uses the \`owner\` access level, the service appends \`ownerId = :currentUserId\` to the query. Administrators bypass the scope. A row owned by somebody else is reported as **404**, not 403, so its existence is not leaked.

## Soft delete

When an entity enables soft delete, \`DELETE /<plural>/:id\` sets \`deletedAt\` instead of removing the row. \`POST /<plural>/:id/restore\` restores it and follows the Delete access rule. Regular queries exclude deleted rows; administrators can pass \`withDeleted=true\`.

Unique constraints still apply to soft-deleted rows: the database does not know a row is "deleted". Either reuse the unique value after a hard delete, or model uniqueness with a partial index outside the generated schema.

## Seeds

\`npm run seed\` creates the configured administrator and three deterministic sample rows per entity. Relations are inserted in dependency order and many-to-many links are added after both sides exist. Re-running the seed is safe: rows are upserted by primary key. Use \`npm run seed -- --reset\` in development to clear generated entity tables first; \`--reset\` is rejected when \`NODE_ENV=production\`.

Note: a seed admin with the default password is for local development only. Change \`ADMIN_PASSWORD\` before exposing the API.

## Environment

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| \`NODE_ENV\` | \`production\` disables schema synchronization and enforces non-default JWT secrets |
| \`PORT\` | HTTP port |
| \`DB_TYPE\` | \`postgres\` |
| \`DB_HOST\`, \`DB_PORT\`, \`DB_USERNAME\`, \`DB_PASSWORD\`, \`DB_DATABASE\` | Database connection |
| \`JWT_ACCESS_SECRET\` | Access token signing secret |
| \`JWT_REFRESH_SECRET\` | Reserved for refresh-token related deployments |
| \`JWT_ACCESS_TTL\`, \`JWT_REFRESH_TTL\` | Token lifetimes (\`15m\`, \`7d\`) |
| \`SEED_ADMIN\`, \`ADMIN_EMAIL\`, \`ADMIN_PASSWORD\` | Initial administrator and deterministic sample data |

## Commands

\`\`\`bash
npm run build
npm run start:prod
npm run test
npm run test:e2e
npm run seed
npm run migration:generate -- src/database/migrations/Init
npm run migration:run
\`\`\`

## Docker

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
# Replace both JWT secrets and ADMIN_PASSWORD in .env first.
docker compose up --build
\`\`\`

The compose stack builds the API, waits for the database health check, runs the
entrypoint and exposes \`http://localhost:3000\`. The container health check calls
\`GET /api/health\`.

| Variable | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| \`RUN_MIGRATIONS\` | Runs \`node dist/database/run-migrations.js\` before the app starts |
| \`RUN_SEED\` | Runs the deterministic seed (admin + sample rows) before the app starts |
| \`DB_SYNCHRONIZE\` | Development convenience; defaults to true in compose. Set to false in production |

For production, generate migrations (\`npm run migration:generate -- src/database/migrations/Init\`),
set \`DB_SYNCHRONIZE=false\` and \`RUN_MIGRATIONS=true\`, and replace every default secret.
",
    "path": "README.md",
  },
  {
    "content": "import { AuthModule } from "./auth/auth.module";
import { JwtAuthGuard } from "./auth/guards/jwt-auth.guard";
import { RolesGuard } from "./auth/guards/roles.guard";
import { AllExceptionsFilter } from "./common/filters/all-exceptions.filter";
import { buildTypeOrmOptions } from "./config/typeorm.config";
import { HealthController } from "./health/health.controller";
import { CommentModule } from "./modules/comment/comment.module";
import { PostModule } from "./modules/post/post.module";
import { TagModule } from "./modules/tag/tag.module";
import { UsersModule } from "./users/users.module";
import { ClassSerializerInterceptor, Module } from "@nestjs/common";
import { ConfigModule, ConfigService } from "@nestjs/config";
import { APP_FILTER, APP_GUARD, APP_INTERCEPTOR } from "@nestjs/core";
import { ThrottlerGuard, ThrottlerModule } from "@nestjs/throttler";
import { TypeOrmModule } from "@nestjs/typeorm";

@Module({
  imports: [
    ConfigModule.forRoot({ isGlobal: true }),
    TypeOrmModule.forRootAsync({
      imports: [ConfigModule],
      inject: [ConfigService],
      useFactory: buildTypeOrmOptions,
    }),
    ThrottlerModule.forRoot([{ ttl: 60_000, limit: 100 }]),
    UsersModule,
    AuthModule,
    PostModule,
    TagModule,
    CommentModule,
  ],
  controllers: [HealthController],
  providers: [
    { provide: APP_GUARD, useClass: ThrottlerGuard },
    { provide: APP_INTERCEPTOR, useClass: ClassSerializerInterceptor },
    { provide: APP_FILTER, useClass: AllExceptionsFilter },
    { provide: APP_GUARD, useClass: JwtAuthGuard },
    { provide: APP_GUARD, useClass: RolesGuard },
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
",
    "path": "src/app.module.ts",
  },
  {
    "content": "import { AuthService } from "./auth.service";
import { CurrentUser } from "./decorators/current-user.decorator";
import { Public } from "./decorators/public.decorator";
import { LoginDto } from "./dto/login.dto";
import { RefreshTokenDto } from "./dto/refresh-token.dto";
import { RegisterDto } from "./dto/register.dto";
import { AuthUser } from "./interfaces/auth-user.interface";
import { Body, Controller, Get, HttpCode, Post } from "@nestjs/common";
import { ApiBearerAuth, ApiTags } from "@nestjs/swagger";
import { Throttle } from "@nestjs/throttler";

@ApiTags("auth")
@Controller("auth")
export class AuthController {
  constructor(private readonly authService: AuthService) {}

  @Public()
  @Throttle({ default: { limit: 5, ttl: 60_000 } })
  @Post("register")
  register(@Body() dto: RegisterDto) {
    return this.authService.register(dto);
  }

  @Public()
  @Throttle({ default: { limit: 5, ttl: 60_000 } })
  @Post("login")
  @HttpCode(200)
  login(@Body() dto: LoginDto) {
    return this.authService.login(dto);
  }

  @Public()
  @Throttle({ default: { limit: 5, ttl: 60_000 } })
  @Post("refresh")
  @HttpCode(200)
  refresh(@Body() dto: RefreshTokenDto) {
    return this.authService.refresh(dto);
  }

  @Public()
  @Throttle({ default: { limit: 10, ttl: 60_000 } })
  @Post("logout")
  @HttpCode(200)
  logout(@Body() dto: RefreshTokenDto) {
    return this.authService.logout(dto);
  }

  @ApiBearerAuth()
  @Get("me")
  me(@CurrentUser() user: AuthUser) {
    return this.authService.me(user.id);
  }
}
",
    "path": "src/auth/auth.controller.ts",
  },
  {
    "content": "import { parseDuration } from "../common/duration";
import { RefreshToken } from "../users/entities/refresh-token.entity";
import { User } from "../users/entities/user.entity";
import { UsersModule } from "../users/users.module";
import { AuthController } from "./auth.controller";
import { AuthService } from "./auth.service";
import { JwtStrategy } from "./strategies/jwt.strategy";
import { Module } from "@nestjs/common";
import { ConfigModule, ConfigService } from "@nestjs/config";
import { JwtModule } from "@nestjs/jwt";
import { PassportModule } from "@nestjs/passport";
import { TypeOrmModule } from "@nestjs/typeorm";

@Module({
  imports: [
    ConfigModule,
    PassportModule.register({ defaultStrategy: "jwt" }),
    JwtModule.registerAsync({
      imports: [ConfigModule],
      inject: [ConfigService],
      useFactory: (config: ConfigService) => ({
        secret: config.get<string>("JWT_ACCESS_SECRET") ?? "change-me-access-secret",
        signOptions: {
          expiresIn: parseDuration(config.get<string>("JWT_ACCESS_TTL") ?? "15m"),
        },
      }),
    }),
    TypeOrmModule.forFeature([User, RefreshToken]),
    UsersModule,
  ],
  controllers: [AuthController],
  providers: [AuthService, JwtStrategy],
  exports: [AuthService],
})
export class AuthModule {}
